{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2122-06-07 22:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Patel. I’ll be taking care of you tonight. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2122-06-07 22:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, yes. I’ve had really high blood sugars all day. Around 5 PM, I got this tightness in my chest, right here in the middle, near my stomach. It scared me, so I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2122-06-07 22:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Was the pain sharp or dull? Did it spread anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2122-06-07 22:05:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It was more pressure than pain. Didn’t move anywhere. It went away after about 15 minutes, but my blood sugar was 706 when I checked after."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2122-06-07 22:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s very high. We’ve confirmed it in the lab. You’re in diabetic ketoacidosis, or DKA. That means your body is producing too many ketones because it doesn’t have enough insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2122-06-07 22:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I’ve been taking my insulin. I don’t understand why this happened."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2122-06-07 22:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sometimes even with good effort, blood sugars can spike. We’ll adjust your insulin while you’re here. Right now, we’re starting an IV insulin drip and giving you fluids to correct the imbalance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2122-06-07 22:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Is the chest pain from my heart?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2122-06-07 22:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your EKG and did blood tests for heart damage. Everything looks normal. The pain might be related to stress or acid in your blood from DKA. It’s not typical heart pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2122-06-07 22:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had it once before when I heard my son was in an accident. Same feeling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2122-06-07 22:18:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That sounds like it could be anxiety-related. We’ll keep an eye on it, but no further heart testing is needed right now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2122-06-07 22:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. My back’s been hurting too. Can I get something for that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2122-06-07 22:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we gave you dilaudid earlier. You’re allergic to morphine and dilaudid, so we used a low dose carefully. We’ll switch to oral pain meds soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2122-06-07 22:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I usually take oxycodone from my regular doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2122-06-07 22:25:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll restart your oral oxycodone once you’re stable. For now, IV helps faster."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2122-06-08 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood sugar is coming down—now 382. Your anion gap is improving, which means the DKA is resolving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2122-06-08 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Is my kidney okay? I remember last time they said I had kidney issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2122-06-08 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine was a bit high at 1.3, but it’s likely from dehydration. With fluids, it’s already improving. No long-term damage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2122-06-08 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. My heart rate’s still high, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2122-06-08 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s in the 110s, which is common in DKA. It should come down as you get more hydrated. EKG shows normal rhythm, no danger signs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2122-06-08 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The endocrine team reviewed your case. We’re stopping the insulin drip and switching you to Lantus at night and Novolog before meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2122-06-08 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that different from what I was on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2122-06-08 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You were on 31 units of Lantus. Now it’s 33. And we’re giving you a sliding scale for Novolog to adjust based on your blood sugar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2122-06-08 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I can do that. Should I check more often?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2122-06-08 14:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, four times a day—before meals and at bedtime. We’ll teach you the scale before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2122-06-09 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are looking good. Anion gap is closed, blood sugar is stable. We’re moving you out of the ICU today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2122-06-09 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great! Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2122-06-09 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. We want to make sure you’re managing your insulin well and your back pain is controlled on oral meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2122-06-09 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been constipated since I’ve been here. Is that from the pain meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2122-06-09 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, oxycodone can cause that. We’ll start a stool softener and encourage fluids and movement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2122-06-10 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure has been low-normal. We held your lisinopril at first, but we’re restarting it today since your kidneys are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2122-06-10 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I take that every day. Was it unsafe to take with the DKA?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2122-06-10 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "In severe dehydration, it can affect kidney function. Now that you’re hydrated, it’s safe to restart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2122-06-10 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been feeling a bit down lately. More than usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2122-06-10 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know managing diabetes can be overwhelming. You’ve had over 20 DKA admissions. Have you had support for anxiety or depression?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2122-06-10 13:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I see someone sometimes, but I’ve missed appointments. It’s hard to keep up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2122-06-10 13:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll make sure your follow-up includes mental health support. It’s just as important as your insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2122-06-11 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Blood sugars are in the 150–200 range. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2122-06-11 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Will I get more insulin to take home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2122-06-11 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You’ll take Lantus 33 units at bedtime and Novolog with meals using the sliding scale we gave you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2122-06-11 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2122-06-11 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue aspirin, lisinopril, Zetia, and Protonix. We switched Protonix to pantoprazole—it’s the same type of medicine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2122-06-11 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m worried about having another episode like this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2122-06-11 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We all are. That’s why follow-up is crucial. Please see your diabetes doctor within a week. They’ll help fine-tune your insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2122-06-11 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my back pain? I don’t have extra oxycodone at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2122-06-11 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We didn’t prescribe more. Please contact your primary doctor to refill it. We don’t restart narcotics at discharge without a review."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2122-06-12 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. Here’s your discharge summary and prescriptions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2122-06-12 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. What should I watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2122-06-12 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your doctor or come back if you have chest pain, shortness of breath, dizziness, or blood sugars over 350 or under 80."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2122-06-12 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’ll make sure to keep my follow-up appointments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2122-06-12 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good plan. Take care, and we’re here if you need us."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2122-06-07 21:51:00",
    "admission_end": "2122-06-12 13:08:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type I diabetes was admitted for diabetic ketoacidosis due to severe hyperglycemia with a blood glucose of 706 and an elevated anion gap. She reported a brief episode of chest tightness, which was evaluated and determined to be non-cardiac, likely related to anxiety or metabolic stress. She was treated with IV fluids and an insulin drip, which was transitioned to subcutaneous Lantus and Novolog. Her renal function, initially impaired due to dehydration, improved with hydration. Her chronic back pain was managed with IV then oral pain medication, but no additional narcotics were provided at discharge. She was discharged home in stable condition with updated insulin dosing and instructions to follow up with her diabetes and primary care providers.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with ketoacidosis, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Diabetes with renal manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Dehydration",
      "Other chest pain",
      "Other specified cardiac dysrhythmias",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Lumbago",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Panic disorder without agoraphobia"
    ]
  }
}
